{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790715817,"nonce":"reGd+x6AysvbddZ2TCdt/LtNu1g=","title":"Preserve qualified enum reflection through Dynamic tokens","message":"`Type.getEnumName(unit.Choice)` returned `Choice`, and `Type.resolveEnum(\"unit.Choice\")` returned null because enum MIR metadata discarded the symbol's package-qualified name. A `unit.Choice` type value stored in `Array\u003cDynamic\u003e` also compared unequal to the same enum type symbol: equality treated its raw runtime ID as a normal Int while the array held a boxed reflective token.\n\nReproducer: `haxe-conformance/regressions/projects/enum_type_reflection`. Before the fix it throws `boxed enum token equality`. With the fix it verifies both equality directions, qualified enum names, and qualified name resolution. In the larger `TestReflect` case, execution proceeds past `testTypes` to later independent `isTrue` failures and a trap-stub crash.\n\nMIR enum metadata now uses the symbol's qualified name. Dynamic equality for class, enum, and interface type symbols compares reflective IDs, preserving the scalar and boxed forms.","files":null}]}